        "original_id": "2214b52a-93d5-5d77-a910-63e375c88315",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Sullivan, Vincenzo Bellini\n- Works: L'Île Enchantée, La Sonnambula\n- Places: Covent Garden\n- Topics: ballet, divertissement, musical works\n\nFacts:\n- In 1864, Arthur Sullivan wrote the ballet L'Île Enchantée.\n- L'Île Enchantée literally means The Enchanted Island.\n- Arthur Sullivan wrote L'Île Enchantée as a divertissement at the end of Vincenzo Bellini's La Sonnambula at Covent Garden.\n- Arthur Sullivan's works include 23 operas, 13 major orchestral works, eight choral works and oratorios, two ballets, incidental music to several plays, numerous hymns and other church pieces, songs, and piano and chamber pieces.",
